WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.810 align:start position:0%
 
see ya  [Applause]  persona 5 is a game overflowing with  style from bold menus that leap off the  screen to the pop and lock of scene  transitions that carry the player around  a colorful Tokyo it's a game about  youthful exuberance and the power that  lies within it but its beauty isn't just  skin deep persona fives gameplay systems  evolve and coalesce over with 80 plus  hours to deliver a confidently executed  role-playing experience that is not only  satisfying but worth the almost  decade-long wait since persona 4 like  its predecessors persona 5 is part  social simulator part dungeon crawler by  day your normal everyday high school  student busy taking classes and hanging  out with friends but by night you are  the leader of the Phantom thieves a  ragtag troupe of idealistic teenagers  that infiltrate a parallel reality  called the meta verse here the corrupted  hearts of adults have manifested as  palaces and the Phantom thieves must  find and steal treasures within them to  reform their marks and by extension  society together with your friends you  infiltrate the meta verse where personas  physical representations of people's  personalities are used to fight with  elemental attacks exploiting a weakness  elevates battles from turn-based  slapsies to a flurry of crushing combos  hitting an enemy's weakness will give  you an additional turn and once they're  all keeled over you can launch an  all-out attack and watch as they are  sliced and diced until they burst into a  shower of blood even though you see it  hundreds of times it never stops being  cool  [Music]  compare the combat in persona 5 pulls  together some of the best elements from  previous games and has been streamlined  into an experience that sings  negotiations from early shin megami  tensei and persona games add another  satisfying wrinkle after downing enemies  you can demand items money or a monsters  allegiance for what you get depends on  your gift of the gab this rework system  let me reap the benefits I needed at  that point in my playthrough while  grinding I'd used an all-out attack to  earn more XP in a pinch I demand an item  it's much more useful than persona 3 in  fours random pickings from shuffle time  the palaces are the best dungeons the  series has ever had they are intricate  striking locations that unravel as you  explore them each varying in size scope  and gameplay opportunities one is a rat  maze filled with locked doors and  looping hallways another is a giant safe  that you need to crack and one is a  crumbling pyramid filled with walking  mummies they feel almost like different  worlds from a Mario game each uniquely  themed and cycling through gameplay  ideas like cards in a rolodex as phantom  thieves you sneak through holes darting  between cover and jumping over obstacles  before ambushing an unsuspecting enemy  and it feels really satisfying when it  works although you're encouraged to take  enemies now sneakily doing so is made  difficult by the game's uncooperative  camera which often restricts your view  while in stealth as a result clambering  over obstacles is unnecessarily finicky  while I find myself accidentally darting  headfirst into a shadow far too often  because the camera betrayed me at the  last second persona 5 has a hefty run  time and while enemies feel well matched  for the majority the gameplay has some  pacing issues towards the end  insta-kill attacks combined with long  stretches of mini boss after mini boss  without a save point mean that the  latter stages can sometimes feel more  frustrating than enjoyable  I've been wiped out half an hour into a  fight on multiple occasions and to be  honest I'm still a little bit bitter but  palaces are just one part of the meta  verse for those that enjoy the grind as  mementos societies joint palace which  takes the  one of Tokyo's subway system this area  is long with many procedurally generated  levels spiralling down towards a  mysterious seemingly unreachable core it  will feel like a monotonous job were it  not for the fan site a website where  members of the public can leave messages  of support or means fansite users can  suggest people they think deserve a  change of heart these are figures that  aren't quite evil enough to have their  own palace but who are still misbehaving  enough to spawn a mini-boss within  mementos these slide stories are mere  tasters bite-sized chunks of justice  that you can dull out to your leisure  while grinding for experience  [Music]  personified creates a rewarding synergy  between its social simulator and  dungeon-crawling by making everyday  activities in the former empower you in  the latter with limited time in each day  and a constant deadline to steal  treasures by it's up to the player to  prioritize after-school and weekend  activities character attributes such as  knowledge proficiency and guts can be  improved by studying working in  part-time jobs or watching DVDs in turn  these enable you to build deeper bonds  with other characters to strengthen  yourself and your cause persona games  live and die on characterization as much  as the RPG mechanics that underpin the  gameplay and in that respect the latest  entry delivers a cast that is lovable  quirky and nuanced in equal measure I  will put my heart and soul into creating  the best nude painting ever what  although the main group neatly fits into  classic anime archetypes initially over  time everyone reveals the baggage they  carry and your affection for them grows  as a result I love that you really had  to invest time and effort into each  character to crack their personality and  work through their pain together these  characters including my favorites  Morgana  the treasure obsessed talking amnesiac  cat and Futaba a hacker with extreme  social anxiety grow and change as you  spend more time with them going from  mechanical tools that you engage with to  strengthen their personas to real people  that you can identify and sympathize  with by the time the credits rolled I  felt like I was leaving behind friends  I'd known for years I heard that real  G's pretty much failed his exams Oh Mona  you little more than any entry in this  series before at persona 5 manages to  make the mundane not only an essential  part of its gameplay loop but also fun  at the same time Atlas has perfected the  back-and-forth investment and reward  dynamic between the games two parts the  real world and the Metaverse to a point  where even doing laundry is gratifying  and how many games can you say that  about  [Music]  persona 5 deals with complex subject  matter and really doesn't shy away from  dark even uncomfortable story beats a  constant theme of the game is oppression  and injustice using personal hardships  and the pressures of modern-day society  to explore how the actions of the older  generation affect the future of the  youth but there's also an optimism to it  all it's cast approaches intricate  issues with a clarity and gusto that can  only be born from teenaged naivety and  there's a refreshing and cathartic  quality to being part of that narrative  Lee Anne thematically persona 5 has the  potential to overwhelm but the writing  does a fantastic job of eliminating  unnecessary exposition to make sure the  important story arcs are clear and that  everyone is on the same page even with  the heavy subject matter little jokes  and Easter eggs mean the mood never  becomes overbearing at every turn  persona 5 presents something to marvel  at whether it's the fluid combat vibrant  world or the many memorable characters  it's a game that I could continue to  talk about for hours I haven't mentioned  the ability to connect to the Thieves  Guild and see how other players spent  their day or the thumping acid jazz  infused soundtrack that I've not been  able to get out of my head but I just  encapsulate why persona 5 is a game that  shouldn't be missed it's stopped a  bursting point with interesting  mechanics and presentation flourishes  there's an overwhelming level of  artistry poured into every part of it  bacon persona 5 a truly landmark entry  in the series it's a refined  effortlessly stylish RPG that will be  talked about for years to come  [Music]  you

